<item>
            <title>[LU-20819] sanity test_130a: OST10 was reported on OST 000a</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20819</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;test_130a and test_130e fail together whenever OSTCOUNT &amp;gt; 9:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  test_130a: OST10 was reported on OST 000a&lt;br/&gt;
  test_130e: OST 000d 1 != 2&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Root cause: both tests compare the OST index from &apos;$LFS getstripe -i&apos; (plain decimal) against the OST index parsed out of &apos;filefrag -ve&apos; output (zero-padded 4-digit, e.g. 000a, 000d) using bash &apos;(( ))&apos; arithmetic. Bash treats a leading-zero operand as octal, so any padded index containing digit 8/9 or a hex letter a-f is not a valid octal/decimal literal: the &apos;(( ))&apos; evaluation itself errors out. In test_130a this makes the equality test spuriously fail; in test_130e it makes the enclosing &apos;if (( $frag_lun != $last_lun ))&apos; silently skip its body, so num_luns never reaches 2. This only shows up once OSTCOUNT exceeds 9 (single-digit indices are octal-safe by luck), which ordinary conf-sanity/sanity runs never do. This change&apos;s own Test-Parameters (osscount=2) bring up 16 OSTs, which is why it surfaces here.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not this patch&apos;s: the diff under review only touches test-framework.sh/functions.sh node-list helpers (nodes_list, facets_nodes, etc.); it makes no change to sanity.sh&apos;s test_130a/test_130e. The same failure signature (OST index &amp;gt;= 8 breaking these comparisons) was already reported against sanity test_130a/130d/130e in 2012 (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-2004&quot; title=&quot;Several sanity 130 test failures&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-2004&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-2004&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, resolved as duplicate), so this predates the patch by well over a decade.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Maloo: &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/2d145c50-18a5-46a6-aaec-ead9ddd73f0f&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/2d145c50-18a5-46a6-aaec-ead9ddd73f0f&lt;/a&gt; (test_130a, test_130e)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-51976-ps6-684d26660414 on &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/51976&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/51976&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
